{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For the poor will never cease from the midst of the land.</b> As I have explained." "<b>To your brother.</b> The one close to you first:" "<b>And to your needy.</b> To the poor of your family and the poor of your land takes precedence over the poor of another place. And the meaning of adjoining it to \"when your brother, a Hebrew, sells himself to you\" — \"you shall surely give to him.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:33.402315235Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}